(7571664, 1215113, 136989, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/>Challenge: I like how the composition first tricked me into thinking symmetry but then slapped me in the face with that point on the right side for the required asymmetry in this challenge.<br/>Technical: Great balance, color and composition. I like how the tower and the lights in the reflection are the only asymmetry.  Very clever.  There''s a bit of rainbow noise in the reflection on the bottom right side.  It''s a minor nit but once I saw it it kept pulling my attention (and I had to find something constructive to add...).<br/>Overall: I''m glad you explained the approach as I was scratching my head to figure that one out. You pulled me in for a closer look, as I tried to figure out how you did it. :)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!Challenge: I like how the composition first tricked me into thinking symmetry but then slapped me in the face with that point on the right side for the required asymmetry in this challenge.Technical: Great balance, color and composition. I like how the tower and the lights in the reflection are the only asymmetry.  Very clever.  There''s a bit of rainbow noise in the reflection on the bottom right side.  It''s a minor nit but once I saw it it kept pulling my attention (and I had to find something constructive to add...).Overall: I''m glad you explained the approach as I was scratching my head to figure that one out. You pulled me in for a closer look, as I tried to figure out how you did it. :)', '2018-06-13 22:34:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7571665, 1215272, 194268, '<td valign="top">Good job!</td>', 'Good job!', '2018-06-13 22:44:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7571682, 1215370, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the HM.</td>', 'Congratulations on the HM.', '2018-06-14 04:02:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7571715, 1215113, 185714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ciaeagle:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/>Challenge: I like how the composition first tricked me into thinking symmetry but then slapped me in the face with that point on the right side for the required asymmetry in this challenge.<br/>Technical: Great balance, color and composition. I like how the tower and the lights in the reflection are the only asymmetry.  Very clever.  There''s a bit of rainbow noise in the reflection on the bottom right side.  It''s a minor nit but once I saw it it kept pulling my attention (and I had to find something constructive to add...).<br/>Overall: I''m glad you explained the approach as I was scratching my head to figure that one out. You pulled me in for a closer look, as I tried to figure out how you did it. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your time analysing what I had captured.  I''m glad too to receive your comments. Truly appreciated.<br/> <br/>cheers<br/>gin :) <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by ciaeagle: Greetings from the Critique Club!Challenge: I like how the composition first tricked me into thinking symmetry but then slapped me in the face with that point on the right side for the required asymmetry in this challenge.Technical: Great balance, color and composition. I like how the tower and the lights in the reflection are the only asymmetry.  Very clever.  There''s a bit of rainbow noise in the reflection on the bottom right side.  It''s a minor nit but once I saw it it kept pulling my attention (and I had to find something constructive to add...).Overall: I''m glad you explained the approach as I was scratching my head to figure that one out. You pulled me in for a closer look, as I tried to figure out how you did it. :)   Thank you for your time analysing what I had captured.  I''m glad too to receive your comments. Truly appreciated. cheersgin :) ', '2018-06-14 11:20:43.000000', NULL, 0),
